.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt DUMPE2FS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dumpe2fs
.Nd list the superblock and block groups of an ext2 file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl bfghixV
.Op Fl o Cm superblock= Ns Ar block
.Op Fl o Cm blocksize= Ns Ar size
.Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the superblock of the ext2 volume on
.Ar device ,
a partition node, a loop device or a file that holds a volume, and then a
section for each block group: where its bitmaps and inode table are, and
its free blocks and inodes.
It only reads.
.Pp
Rach2 uses e2fsprogs 1.47.4, linked statically against the ported musl,
and installs it on the GNU system at
.Pa /sbin/dumpe2fs .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b
Print the blocks the volume records as bad.
.It Fl f
Print a volume whose features
.Nm
does not know.
.It Fl g
Print each group as one line of fields separated by colons.
.It Fl h
Print the superblock alone.
.It Fl i
Read an image
.Ql e2image
made; no image of the kind is made on Rach2, which does not build
e2image.
.It Fl o Cm superblock= Ns Ar block
Read the superblock at
.Ar block ,
a backup.
.It Fl o Cm blocksize= Ns Ar size
The block size to read the backup with.
.It Fl x
Print block numbers in hexadecimal.
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success and 1 on an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The features and the block size of the root:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# dumpe2fs -h /dev/disk0p3 | grep -E 'features|Block size'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr e2fsck 8 ,
.Xr mke2fs 8 ,
.Xr tune2fs 8
